Keanu Reeves voluntarily slashed his salary by approximately $2 million for the 1997 film “The Devil’s Advocate” so producers could afford Al Pacino’s higher asking price. Reeves believed Pacino’s involvement was essential for the movie’s success, and Pacino later matched the gesture by donating an equivalent amount to charity.

